{"raw": {"https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201864354637_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Part Time Spanish Instructor", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nOhio Wesleyan University is a selective, private, undergraduate liberal arts institution founded in 1842 and located just 20 miles north of Columbus. The Department of World Languages and Cultures at Ohio Wesleyan University is seeking one part-time Spanish Instructor to teach two sections of second-semester Spanish, with a strong likelihood of teaching one section of first-semester Spanish during the Spring 2027 semester. These courses are taught on campus and meet four times per week for 50 minutes each session on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Fridays. There may also be an opportunity to teach during the Fall 2027 semester. The ideal candidate will possess a master's degree in Spanish or Foreign Language Education, native or near-native fluency in Spanish, and prior college-level teaching experience. As a residential liberal arts institution, Ohio Wesleyan University delivers all instruction in a face-to-face, in-person environment. Online courses are not offered during the fall and spring semesters. Compensation is $5,000 per course. This position is not eligible for benefits. If you decide to join the Dept. of World Languages and Cultures , you will: Become part of a dynamic, supportive, and collaborative team of instructors who are committed to their students and to excellence in language teaching.\u00a0 Join a liberal arts college that is deeply committed to creating an environment that acknowledges, encourages, and celebrates differences.\u00a0 Teach small classes (up to 22 students per class). Be mentored by and receive support from the Chair and other members of the department as needed. Have office space for use while you are on campus. Receive a free parking pass that allows you to park anywhere on campus. To apply, please submit a cover letter expressing your interest in the position and a current curriculum vitae, including the names and contact information of three professional references, to Dr. Eva Paris\u00a0 ( eeparish@owu.edu ),\u00a0 Chair of the Department of World Languages and Cultures. The Spring 2027 semester begins on Wednesday, January 13, 2027. Applications will be reviewed as they are received and will be accepted until the position is filled. Ohio Wesleyan University offers a rewarding place to work. To learn more about why OWU could be your next professional home, please visit\u00a0 our website .", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201858549405_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Public Safety Officer Part Time", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nOhio Wesleyan University \u00a0( www.owu.edu ) is a selective, private, undergraduate liberal arts, residential institution founded in 1842 and is located just 20 miles north of Columbus. The University\u2019s Department of Public Safety invites applications for a Part-Time Public Safety Officer. This is a 20 hour a week position that works a varying schedule.\u00a0 POSITION SUMMARY: As a non-sworn Public Safety Officer, you will be on a small team with big responsibilities - taking action when unsafe behaviors are observed and responding to emergency situations. We will rely on you to handle calls across the entire campus, deter crime, and build meaningful relationships. To thrive in this position, you will make our community feel safe, supported, and treated equitably. We pay $20/hr. This position benefits those who need or like non-traditional work schedules. Most shifts involve evening or night hours and may include weekends. Over time, employees with seniority may select shifts with more traditional hours. STARTING QUALIFICATIONS: Age Requirement: Must be at least 21 years of age at the time of hire Education : \u00a0High school diploma or GED required Experience: \u00a0Minimum 1 to 2 years of experience in customer service, social work, psychology, security, public safety, or working with young adults/student populations Interpersonal Skills: \u00a0Exceptional communication skills, empathy, conflict resolution, and active listening skills with a strong customer-service focus. Ability to work well in a team environment Physical Requirements: \u00a0Ability to stand and walk for extended periods, sit and operate a vehicle, climb stairs during building checks, and work outdoors in varying weather conditions Candidates must have an Ohio driver license\u00a0 Candidates must pass a Background Check screening Hours: \u00a0Part-time (typically 10 to 29 hours per week; flexible, variable shifts including evenings, weekends, and nights) \u00a0 Key Responsibilities Patrol & Parking Enforcement Enforce campus parking regulations, issue citations, and manage special event traffic routing. Conduct regular vehicle and foot patrols of academic buildings, residence halls, athletic facilities, and exterior grounds. Check and secure doors, windows, and facility entry points at designated intervals. Monitor campus property for safety hazards, maintenance issues, and suspicious activities or unauthorized persons. Student Engagement & Support Build positive, trusting relationships with students, faculty, and staff. Serve as a friendly, approachable campus resource and first point of contact for student needs or directions. Assist students with lockouts for residence halls and campus buildings upon verification of proper identification. Emergency Response & Policy Support Enforce and abide by all university policies, rules, and regulations with a de-escalation and education-first mindset. Respond promptly to campus calls, alarms, and routine requests for assistance. Contact and act as a professional liaison with local emergency services (police, fire, 911) when necessary. Administrative Duties Document all daily activities, shift logs, and security occurrences accurately. Write clear, objective incident, citation, and damage reports using computerized reporting software. \u00a0 FACTORS CONTRIBUTING SUCCESS:\u00a0 You use your wit and emotional intelligence to de-escalate situations You value diverse cultures and learning from others People feel heard and understood by you through active listening and non-verbal body language You evaluate and pick your methods of communication appropriate to situations - ranging from a voice of empathy to measured authority You don\u2019t just say you have a passion for serving others - you act on it You are able to write clearly and concisely Completed application packets will include: Letter of interest (cover letter) Resume or Curriculum Vitae\u00a0 The names, titles, and contact information for three professional references NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Please email application materials to: jobs@owu.edu Application review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.\u00a0 WHAT WE OFFER: Located in the Columbus, Ohio metropolitan area, Ohio Wesleyan is a selective residential liberal arts college enrolling approximately 1,600+ students. The college\u2019s signature program, The OWU Connection, empowers students to complete research, community service, careers, and study abroad, teaching students to apply their knowledge in real-world settings. Ohio Wesleyan is featured in the book Colleges That Change Lives and was recently listed as the No. 1 liberal arts college in Ohio for social mobility by U.S. News and World Report. OWU is located in Delaware, OH, a lively college town just 30 minutes from Columbus, the 14th most populous city in the United States and part of the fastest growing, most economically vibrant areas of the Midwest. Columbus, known increasingly as the \u201cSilicon Midwest,\u201d was named by LinkedIn as one of the top 10 U.S. cities in which to launch your career. \u00a0 To achieve our mission, we continually strive to foster a campus community where every individual is respected, supported, and able to flourish. We affirm the worth of all persons and welcome people of all backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences. Ohio Wesleyan University is an equal opportunity institution and seeks applications from individuals who will contribute to, and help strengthen, our commitment to academic excellence, mutual respect, and the shared pursuit of knowledge.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201856646448_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Data Science Research Assistant-SW", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nPurpose/Objective of the Role:\u00a0 The Data Lab is seeking two motivated students to assist with a real-world analytics project for a water utility company. This position places a strong emphasis on research, specifically identifying the right datasets and determining which factors most significantly influence model performance in the context of utility management and resource optimization. The successful candidates will work independently to extract insights and build predictive models that could have tangible industry impact. \u00a0 \u00a0 Tasks & Responsibilities: \u00a0 Data Discovery & Research:\u00a0 Investigate potential data sources to determine the most suitable data for specific research problems related to water utility operations.\u00a0 Data Exploration & Analysis:\u00a0 Perform Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) to understand data structure.\u00a0 Feature Selection: Analyze data to identify key variables and determine which factors influence the model's accuracy.\u00a0 Model Building:\u00a0 Design, implement, and validate predictive models using appropriate machine learning algorithms.\u00a0 Documentation:\u00a0 Clearly document all research methods, data sources, and results for future reference.\u00a0 Qualifications/Skills: Education:\u00a0 Currently enrolled as an undergraduate major in Data Analytics, Computer Science or Mathematics.\u00a0 Coursework:\u00a0 Successful completion of CS 300: Data Mining and Machine Learning (or equivalent coursework/experience).\u00a0 Technical Skills:\u00a0 Experience with Python-based data science libraries (e.g., NumPy, pandas, scikit-learn) is preferred.\u00a0 Soft Skills:\u00a0 Ability to work independently, manage time effectively, and document work clearly.\u00a0 Potential Future Career Benefits:\u00a0 Industry Application:\u00a0 Apply theoretical knowledge to a live industry project with a water utility company, bridging the gap between classroom learning and real-world application.\u00a0 End-to-End Data Science Skills:\u00a0 Gain proficiency in the full data lifecycle, from data discovery and cleaning to feature selection and model building.\u00a0 Portfolio Building:\u00a0 Generate tangible results and research experience that can be discussed in future job interviews.\u00a0 Mentorship:\u00a0 Work directly with faculty to refine your technical and research methodologies.\u00a0 \u00a0 NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States Application Instructions:\u00a0 Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: Mehwish Abbasi Commitment: 5-8 hours per week Term: Fall 2026 only", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201853792179_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Accounting Operations Strategic Automation Specialist", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nStrengthen financial operations. Modernize processes. Create measurable impact. DEPARTMENT Accounting REPORTS TO Controller APPOINTMENT Full-time | 12 months Help shape the future of financial operations at Ohio Wesleyan Ohio Wesleyan University is seeking an experienced, forward-thinking Accounting Operations & Strategic Automation Specialist to strengthen our financial operations while helping us modernize the way work gets done. This is an opportunity for an accounting or financial operations professional who combines strong technical knowledge with curiosity, initiative, and a passion for continuous improvement. You will provide leadership for essential accounting functions - including accounts payable, purchasing, reconciliations, and financial close activities - while identifying ways to use automation, data analytics, and AI-enabled tools to reduce manual work, improve accuracy, and support better decision-making. The successful candidate will be comfortable moving between day-to-day financial operations and broader strategic initiatives. You will collaborate with colleagues across the University, assess current processes, develop practical improvements, and help build a culture that embraces innovation, efficiency, and responsible financial stewardship. What You'll Do Strengthen accounting and financial operations Support accurate financial reconciliations and proactively identify and resolve variances. Establish, maintain, and continuously improve reconciliation procedures and timelines. Support timely monthly reporting and year-end close and audit activities. Oversee accounts payable and procurement processes, including invoice processing, vendor management, payment practices, and cash-flow considerations. Provide lead direction and guidance to assigned staff and student employees. Advance strategic sourcing and cost optimization Analyze University spending to identify cost-saving opportunities, purchasing efficiencies, duplicate vendors, and opportunities to consolidate services. Support requests for proposals for major purchasing categories, evaluate vendor responses, and recommend sourcing strategies aligned with University priorities. Monitor contract renewals, vendor performance, cost increases, and related budget impacts. Strengthen vendor relationships while improving payment terms, processes, and financial visibility. Lead automation and process modernization Identify, design, and implement automation opportunities across accounting and financial workflows. Develop automated accounts payable entry, approval, and payment processes, including ACH, wire, and check workflows with improved tracking. Use data analytics, exception reporting, intelligent matching, and standardized templates to improve reconciliation processes. Explore practical uses of AI-enabled accounting tools, robotic process automation, and other emerging technologies. Partner with Finance, Information Services, budget managers, and other campus colleagues to ensure that technology recommendations support institutional priorities and include appropriate training and resources. Help colleagues understand and adopt new processes by building engagement, providing guidance, and demonstrating the value of change. What You'll Bring Required qualifications Bachelor's degree in accounting, finance, business administration, or a related field. Seven to ten years of progressively responsible experience in accounting, financial operations, procurement, strategic sourcing, or a closely related area. Strong proficiency with ERP systems, financial software, electronic procurement platforms, and advanced Microsoft Excel functions, including pivot tables and lookup functions. Demonstrated success designing and implementing process improvements, automation, or system enhancements. Experience using - or the ability to effectively evaluate and apply - AI-enabled accounting tools and emerging automation technologies. Strong financial and analytical skills, including the ability to assess costs and benefits, evaluate contracts, monitor performance measures, and translate data into recommendations. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to manage multiple complex projects and priorities with limited direction. A collaborative, customer-service-focused, and solution-oriented approach. Additional experience that will help you succeed Accounting, procurement, or financial operations experience in higher education or another complex organization. Experience with expense management systems such as Concur. Experience with accounts payable automation or electronic procurement platforms such as Jaggaer. Experience leading change initiatives, building organizational support, and encouraging innovation. Experience providing direction or guidance to staff or student employees. Why This Role Matters The work of this position will have an impact across the University. By strengthening core accounting practices, improving purchasing decisions, and thoughtfully applying technology, the Accounting Operations & Strategic Automation Specialist will help Ohio Wesleyan: Improve the accuracy and timeliness of financial information. Reduce repetitive and manual work. Strengthen vendor and purchasing practices. Identify meaningful cost-saving opportunities. Improve service to campus partners. Build more responsive, efficient, and sustainable financial operations. If you are energized by the opportunity to combine accounting expertise, strategic thinking, and emerging technology to create measurable organizational improvements, we encourage you to apply. To Apply Completed application packets must include: A letter of interest A cover letter A current resume The names, titles, and contact information for three professional references who may be contacted later in the selection process. References will not be contacted without the candidate's prior awareness. Candidates who experience difficulty uploading all required materials through our career page may submit supplemental materials to jobs@owu.edu . Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Work authorization:\u00a0 Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. What We Offer Ohio Wesleyan is a selective, residential liberal arts college enrolling approximately 1,600 students. The college's signature program, The OWU Connection , empowers students to complete research, community service, career experiences, and study abroad, teaching students to apply their knowledge in real-world settings. Ohio Wesleyan is featured in the book Colleges That Change Lives and was recently listed by U.S. News & World Report as the No. 1 liberal arts college in Ohio for social mobility. To discover why Ohio Wesleyan offers a rewarding place to work - and why it could be your next work home - visit our What Makes Working at OWU Great webpage. OWU is located in Delaware, Ohio, a lively college town just 30 minutes north of Columbus - the 14th most populous city in the United States and part of one of the fastest-growing, most economically vibrant regions in the Midwest. Columbus, increasingly known as the \"Silicon Midwest,\" was named by LinkedIn as one of the top 10 U.S. cities in which to launch a career. Our Commitment To achieve our mission, we continually strive to foster a campus community where every individual is respected, supported, and able to flourish. We affirm the worth of all persons and welcome people of all backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences. Ohio Wesleyan University is an equal opportunity institution and seeks applications from individuals who will contribute to and help strengthen our commitment to academic excellence, mutual respect, and the shared pursuit of knowledge.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201853728794_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Psychology\u2013Applied Psychology", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nAssistant Professor of Psychology \u2013 Applied Psychology The\u00a0 Department of Psychology\u00a0 at Ohio Wesleyan University invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professorship in an applied area of psychology, such as Industrial/Organizational (I/O) Psychology or Human Factors starting in August 2027. We are seeking candidates committed to excellent undergraduate teaching and to developing a vibrant research program that involves undergraduates of all backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences. The successful candidate will join a\u00a0 departmental community \u00a0with a wide range of research and teaching interests and will benefit from extensive support for junior faculty, including start-up funding, pre-tenure research leave, funding for student-faculty research collaboration via the\u00a0 Summer Scholarship & Research Program \u00a0and\u00a0 The OWU Connection , and a range of workshops and mentoring programs supported by the endowed\u00a0 Smith Center for Faculty Excellence .\u00a0 This job is part of a cluster of positions focused on flexibility, interdisciplinarity, and inclusivity. The faculty cohort will join an educational community that values interdisciplinarity and fosters close working relationships with students through our signature program in experiential learning, the OWU Connection. Incoming faculty will be provided with mentoring, professional development, funds, and opportunities to connect with faculty across the\u00a0 Ohio 5\u00a0 and\u00a0 GLCA consortia . For more information about the cluster, please visit\u00a0 www.owu.edu/joinOWUfaculty . Responsibilities Teaching three courses per semester including Introduction to Psychology (PSYC 110) and Organizational Psychology (PSYC 264) Advising students in their academic journey Engaging in a consistent and focused line of research.\u00a0 Providing service to the department, university, and profession Assisting in curriculum development, revision, and evaluation Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Psychology or a related discipline Evidence of preparation for teaching at the undergraduate level Interest in or experience with mentoring undergraduate researchers. Application Requirements Applicants should submit the following:\u00a0 Cover Letter CV Teaching and Student Engagement Statement (4-page limit): \u00a0 Please provide a statement that articulates your teaching philosophy. In your response, address your ability to teach a broad range of courses and to employ pedagogical approaches that support students with varied perspectives and experiences. Describe how you connect students with opportunities, resources, and networks that expand their access to your field of study. Include examples of outreach, advising, or program activities that have supported students whose pathways into the discipline may not follow a traditional trajectory. Research statement (2-page limit): a statement outlining the central aims of the research program you would like to develop and how it will thrive at Ohio Wesleyan. Please describe how you would incorporate undergraduates in your research.\u00a0 Please submit all materials via\u00a0 www.owu.edu/joinOWUfaculty , where you will find additional information about working at OWU. Official transcripts, reference letters, and additional materials may be requested at a later time, and can be sent directly to\u00a0 facultyjobs@owu.edu . Please make sure to include \u201cPsychology\u201d in the subject line. Review of applications will begin o n October 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled.\u00a0 About Ohio Wesleyan\u00a0 Located in the Columbus, Ohio metropolitan area, Ohio Wesleyan is a selective \u00a0 residential liberal arts college enrolling approximately 1,600+ students from across the nation and around the world. The college\u2019s signature program,\u00a0 the OWU Connection , empowers students to complete research, community service, careers, and study abroad, teaching students to apply their knowledge in real-world settings. Ohio Wesleyan is featured in the book\u00a0 Colleges That Change Lives \u00a0and was recently listed as the No. 1 liberal arts college in Ohio for social mobility by\u00a0 U.S. News and World Report . OWU is located in Delaware, OH, a lively college town just 30 minutes from Columbus, the 14th most populous city in the United States and part of the fastest growing, most economically vibrant areas of the Midwest. Columbus, known increasingly as the \u201cSilicon Midwest,\u201d was named by LinkedIn as one of the top 10 U.S. cities in which to launch your career. To achieve our mission, we continually strive to foster a campus community where every individual is respected, supported, and able to flourish. We affirm the worth of all persons and welcome people of all backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences. Ohio Wesleyan University is an equal opportunity institution and seeks applications from individuals who will contribute to, and help strengthen, our commitment to academic excellence, mutual respect, and the shared pursuit of knowledge.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201853725566_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Accounting and Finance", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nAssistant Professor of Accounting and Finance - Department of Economics and Business Position Description\u00a0 The\u00a0 Department of Economics and Business \u00a0at\u00a0 Ohio Wesleyan University \u00a0invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professorship in Accounting and Finance beginning August 2027. We seek an outstanding teacher who (1) possesses expertise in accounting or finance and a background in integrating the two disciplines; and (2) is committed to engaging undergraduates in the classroom and in related campus programming through the Woltemade Center, the Accounting and Finance Fellows program, and the Delaware Entrepreneurial Center. The successful candidate will join a departmental and interdisciplinary community with a wide range of research and teaching interests and will benefit from extensive support for junior faculty, including access to the\u00a0 Smith Center for Faculty Excellence , start-up funding, pre-tenure research leave, funding for student-faculty research collaboration via the\u00a0 Summer Scholarship and Research Program \u00a0and\u00a0 The OWU Connection , and a range of workshops and mentoring programs.\u00a0 This job is part of a cluster of positions focused on flexibility, interdisciplinarity, and inclusivity. The faculty cohort will join an educational community that values interdisciplinarity and fosters close working relationships with students through our signature program in experiential learning, the OWU Connection. Incoming faculty will be provided with mentoring, professional development, funds, and opportunities to connect with faculty across the\u00a0 Ohio 5 \u00a0 and\u00a0 GLCA consortia . For more information about the cluster, please visit\u00a0 www.owu.edu/joinOWUfaculty . Responsibilities: Teach six courses annually (3/3) in accounting and finance at the introductory, intermediate and advanced levels, potentially including introduction to financial accounting, financial statement analysis, financial management, and related topics reflecting both the candidate\u2019s expertise and the needs of the department and program. \u00a0On average, the faculty member will teach four courses annually in accounting and two courses annually in finance, depending on the department\u2019s needs. Collaborate with colleagues in the Department of Economics and Business to advance a shared vision for extraordinary student outcomes and growth across supported programs. Support department co-curricular groups and activities as appropriate, such as the Woltemade Economics and Business Fellows. Engage in a consistent and focused line of research. Advise students in their academic journey. Provide service to the department, university, and profession. Assist in curriculum development, revision, and evaluation. \u00a0 Qualifications: Masters of Accountancy, MBA, or doctorate in accounting, finance, or a related field Professional experience in accounting and/or finance Evidence of preparation for teaching at the undergraduate level \u00a0 Application Materials Applicants should submit: Cover letter Current CV Teaching and student engagement statement \u00a0(3-page limit): Please provide a statement that articulates your teaching philosophy. In your response, address your ability to teach a broad range of courses and to employ pedagogical approaches that support students with varied perspectives and experiences. Describe how you connect students with opportunities, resources, and networks that expand their access to your field of study. Include examples of outreach, advising, or program activities that have supported students whose pathways into the discipline may not follow a traditional trajectory. Please submit all materials via\u00a0 www.owu.edu/joinOWUfaculty , where you will find additional information about working at OWU. Official transcripts, reference letters, and additional materials may be requested at a later time and can be sent directly to\u00a0 facultyjobs@owu.edu . Please make sure to include \u201cEconomics and Business\u2013Accounting and Finance\" in the subject line. Review of applications will begin on October 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. About Ohio Wesleyan Located in the Columbus, Ohio metropolitan area, Ohio Wesleyan is a selective residential liberal arts college enrolling approximately 1,600+ students from across the nation and around the world. The college\u2019s signature program,\u00a0 the \u00a0OWU Connection , empowers students to complete research, community service, careers, and study abroad, teaching students to apply their knowledge in real-world settings. Ohio Wesleyan is featured in the book Colleges That Change Lives and was recently listed as the No. 1 liberal arts college in Ohio for social mobility by U.S. News and World Report. OWU is located in Delaware, OH, a lively college town just 30 minutes from Columbus, the 14th most populous city in the United States and part of the fastest growing, most economically vibrant areas of the Midwest. Columbus, known increasingly as the \u201cSilicon Midwest,\u201d was named by LinkedIn as one of the top 10 U.S. cities in which to launch your career. To achieve our mission, we continually strive to foster a campus community where every individual is respected, supported, and able to flourish. We affirm the worth of all persons and welcome people of all backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences. Ohio Wesleyan University is an equal opportunity institution and seeks applications from individuals who will contribute to, and help strengthen, our commitment to academic excellence, mutual respect, and the shared pursuit of knowledge", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201853722436_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Biological Sciences-Neuroscience", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nAssistant Professor of Biological Sciences \u2013 Neuroscience The\u00a0 Department of Biological Sciences \u00a0at Ohio Wesleyan University invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professorship in Neuroscience ( OWU Neuroscience Program ) starting in August 2027. We are seeking candidates committed to excellent undergraduate teaching and to developing a vibrant research program that involves undergraduates of all experience levels and backgrounds. We are especially interested in candidates with research experience in neurobiology. The successful candidate will join a departmental and interdisciplinary community with a wide range of research and teaching interests and will benefit from extensive support for junior faculty, including access to the\u00a0 Smith Center for Faculty Excellence , start-up funding, pre-tenure research leave, funding for student-faculty research collaboration via the\u00a0 Summer Scholarship and Research Program \u00a0and\u00a0 The OWU Connection , and a range of workshops and mentoring programs.\u00a0 This job is part of a cluster of positions focused on flexibility, interdisciplinarity, and inclusivity. The faculty cohort will join an educational community that values interdisciplinarity and fosters close working relationships with students through our signature program in experiential learning, the OWU Connection. Incoming faculty will be provided with mentoring, professional development, funds, and opportunities to connect with faculty across the\u00a0 Ohio 5 \u00a0 and\u00a0 GLCA consortia . For more information about the cluster, please visit\u00a0 www.owu.edu/joinOWUfaculty . Responsibilities Teaching three to four courses (9 to 12 contact hours) a semester Teaching Introduction to Neuroscience (NEUR 110), Topics in Neuroscience (NEUR 374), Molecular and Cellular Neuroscience (NEUR 362), and contributing to the required Introduction to Cell Biology (BIOL 120) Contribute to teaching one or more of the following: Human Physiology (BIOL 325), Genetics (BIOL 271), or Cell and Molecular Biology (BIOL 351) Advising students in their academic journey Engaging in a consistent and focused line of research\u00a0 in neurobiology Providing service to the department, university, and profession Assisting in curriculum development, revision, and evaluation Qualifications Ph.D. in Neuroscience or a related discipline Evidence of preparation for teaching at the undergraduate level A research program in neurobiology or related discipline Application Materials Applicants should submit the following required materials:\u00a0 Cover Letter CV Teaching and student engagement statement (3-page limit): Please provide a statement that articulates your teaching philosophy. In your response, address your ability to teach a broad range of courses and to employ pedagogical approaches that support students with varied perspectives and experiences. Describe how you connect students with opportunities, resources, and networks that expand their access to your field of study. Include examples of outreach, advising, or program activities that have supported students whose pathways into the discipline may not follow a traditional trajectory. Research statement (2-page limit): a statement outlining the central aims of the research program you would like to develop and how it will thrive at Ohio Wesleyan. If you intend to use an animal model, please describe the housing facilities and support staff that you anticipate needing to conduct your research on campus. Please submit all materials via\u00a0 www.owu.edu/joinOWUfaculty , where you will find additional information about working at OWU. Official transcripts, reference letters, and additional materials may be requested at a later time and can be sent directly to\u00a0 facultyjobs@owu.edu . Please make sure to include \u201cBiological Sciences - Neuroscience\u201d in the subject line. Review of applications will begin on \u00a0October 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled.\u00a0 About Ohio Wesleyan\u00a0 Located in the Columbus, Ohio metropolitan area, Ohio Wesleyan is a selective residential liberal arts college enrolling approximately 1,600+ students from across the nation and around the world. The college\u2019s signature program,\u00a0 the \u00a0OWU Connection , empowers students to complete research, community service, careers, and study abroad, teaching students to apply their knowledge in real-world settings. Ohio Wesleyan is featured in the book Colleges That Change Lives and was recently listed as the No. 1 liberal arts college in Ohio for social mobility by U.S. News and World Report. OWU is located in Delaware, OH, a lively college town just 30 minutes from Columbus, the 14th most populous city in the United States and part of the fastest growing, most economically vibrant areas of the Midwest. Columbus, known increasingly as the \u201cSilicon Midwest,\u201d was named by LinkedIn as one of the top 10 U.S. cities in which to launch your career. To achieve our mission, we continually strive to foster a campus community where every individual is respected, supported, and able to flourish. We affirm the worth of all persons and welcome people of all backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences. Ohio Wesleyan University is an equal opportunity institution and seeks applications from individuals who will contribute to, and help strengthen, our commitment to academic excellence, mutual respect, and the shared pursuit of knowledge", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201853717615_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Data Analytics", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nAssistant Professor of Data Analytics Ohio Wesleyan University\u2019s\u00a0 Data Analytics program \u00a0invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Data Analytics to begin in August 2027. We seek an enthusiastic colleague and instructor with deep professional experience in a range of disciplinary Data Analytics applications. We encourage applicants from any academic field (e.g., social sciences, humanities, or natural sciences) that possess strong data analytics expertise and experience to apply. OWU\u2019s Data Analytics program is an interdisciplinary program grounded in the liberal arts. In addition to courses in Data Analytics, Mathematics, and Computer Science, students also study in several cognate disciplines, including Politics and Government, Psychology, Physics, Geography, Finance, Environmental Studies, Economics,\u00a0 Anthropology and Sociology,\u00a0 and Accounting. Throughout, students consider the ethical implications of their work and develop problem-solving skills that draw upon habits and methods of a range of disciplines. The successful candidate will join a faculty and interdisciplinary community with a wide range of research and teaching interests and will benefit from extensive support for junior faculty, including start-up funding, pre-tenure research leave, funding for student-faculty research collaboration via the\u00a0 Summer Scholarship & Research Program \u00a0and\u00a0 The OWU Connection , and a range of workshops and mentoring programs supported by the endowed\u00a0 Smith Center for Faculty Excellence .\u00a0 This job is part of a cluster of positions focused on flexibility, interdisciplinarity, and inclusivity. The faculty cohort will join an educational community that values interdisciplinarity and fosters close working relationships with students through our signature program in experiential learning, the OWU Connection. Incoming faculty will be provided with mentoring, professional development, funds, and opportunities to connect with faculty across the\u00a0 Ohio 5 \u00a0and\u00a0 GLCA consortia . For more information about the cluster, please visit\u00a0 www.owu.edu/joinOWUfaculty . . Responsibilities Collaborate in teaching six program or department courses a year (3/3), including several existing DATA courses such as Introduction to Data Analytics, Social, Ethical, and Cultural Impacts of Big Data, Data Visualization and Presentation, Methods in Data Analytics, and Capstone. Assist in developing and expanding OWU\u2019s Data Analytics program, including the creation of new classes in Data Analytics or in a cognate discipline. Advise and mentor students in their academic journey. Engage in a consistent and focused line of research. Provide service to the program, university, and profession. Assist in curriculum development, revision, and evaluation. Qualifications Ph.D. or Master\u2019s degree in analytics, data science, or a related field Evidence of preparation for teaching at the undergraduate level. Interest in or experience with mentoring undergraduates, including students entering data analytics from a range of academic backgrounds and levels of preparation. A research agenda in data analytics or a related field. Application Materials Applicants should submit the following: Cover Letter CV Teaching and Student Engagement Statement (2-page limit): Please provide a statement that articulates your teaching philosophy. In your response, address your ability to teach a broad range of courses and to employ pedagogical approaches that support students with varied perspectives and experiences. Describe how you connect students with opportunities, resources, and networks that expand their access to your field of study. Include examples of outreach, advising, or program activities that have supported students whose pathways into the discipline may not follow a traditional trajectory. Research statement (2-page limit): A statement outlining the central aims of the research program you would like to develop, how it will thrive at Ohio Wesleyan, and how you will involve OWU students in your research. Please submit all materials via\u00a0 www.owu.edu/joinOWUfaculty , where you will find additional information about working at OWU. Official transcripts, reference letters, and additional materials may be requested at a later time, and can be sent directly to\u00a0 facultyjobs@owu.edu . Please make sure to include \u201cData Analytics\u201d in the subject line. Questions may be directed to Mehwish Abbasi, search chair\u00a0 (mabbasi@owu.edu) . Review of applications will begin on October 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. About Ohio Wesleyan Located in the Columbus, Ohio metropolitan area, Ohio Wesleyan is a selective \u00a0 residential liberal arts college enrolling approximately 1,600+ students from across the nation and around the world. The college\u2019s signature program,\u00a0 the OWU Connection , empowers students to complete research, community service, careers, and study abroad, teaching students to apply their knowledge in real-world settings. Ohio Wesleyan is featured in the book\u00a0 Colleges That Change Lives \u00a0and was recently listed as the No. 1 liberal arts college in Ohio for social mobility by\u00a0 U.S. News and World Report . OWU is located in Delaware, OH, a lively college town just 30 minutes from Columbus, the 14th most populous city in the United States and part of the fastest growing, most economically vibrant areas of the Midwest. Columbus, known increasingly as the \u201cSilicon Midwest,\u201d was named by LinkedIn as one of the top 10 U.S. cities in which to launch your career.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201845493393_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Student Worker - Athletics", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-13\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nAthletics-SW The OWU Athletics Department is looking to hire Student Workers Athletics Game Management\u00a0 SQ Fitness Center\u00a0 Morrill Fitness Center\u00a0 \u00a0 Summary: The Athletics Department is seeking enthusiastic and reliable student workers to assist in supporting the daily operations, events, and activities within the department. This position provides students with the opportunity to gain valuable experience in a fast-paced and dynamic environment while contributing to the success of our athletic programs. \u00a0 Tasks & Responsibilities:\u00a0 Game Management:\u00a0 This position will assist with various gameday operational positions at home athletic events. Positions include game presentation roles (music, video board, scoreboard, PA, etc.), implementing in-game promotions, sideline ball helpers, setup and teardown of events, as well as other duties as needed.\u00a0 \u00a0 SQ/Morrill Fitness Center: This position serves as the primary customer service representative for the Simpson-Querrey Fitness Center and/or Morrill Strength & Conditioning Room and is responsible for:\u00a0 Greeting and welcoming members/guests with a smile and friendly attitude. Upholding, enforcing and clearly communicating rules and regulations of fitness center.\u00a0 Performing duties at desks; including, but not limited to checking IDs to ensure proper patron access to facility, rental of recreational equipment, and maintaining user counts.\u00a0 Monitoring, organizing and cleaning the fitness center (including workspace); maintaining a presentable environment for users.\u00a0 Performing laundry of towels, as well as re-filling equipment cleaning bottles.\u00a0 Attending any required meetings or training sessions.\u00a0 Regular attendance of assigned shifts.\u00a0 Additional Responsibilities: Event Support: Assist with game-day operations, including setup and teardown of equipment, ticketing, concessions, and crowd management. Customer Service: Greet and assist guests, athletes, and staff, providing information and addressing inquiries professionally.\u00a0 Help maintain athletic facilities, ensuring cleanliness, organization, and readiness for practices, games, and events. Equipment Management: Organize and distribute athletic gear, maintain inventory, and assist in equipment upkeep. Marketing and Promotions: Support the promotion of athletic events through social media, flyer distribution, and event signage. Other Duties: Complete additional tasks as assigned by supervisors to support the department\u2019s operations.\u00a0 Any previous experience working athletic events is preferred, but not required.\u00a0 Must be dependable, and be able to work nights and weekends. Comfortable standing, walking, and performing physical tasks for extended periods. Other tasks as assigned. NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States Application Instructions:\u00a0 Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: Abby Stoner Commitment: 15-20 hours per week Term: Fall 26 & Spring 27, part-time position", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200985587928_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Student Worker - ECC Crossing Guard", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-05\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nStudent Worker \u2013 ECC Crossing Guard Purpose/Objective of the Role: The Service Learning office and the Early Childhood Center (ECC) are partnering to make Park Ave safer for our preschool program! We are hiring students each semester to serve as Crossing Guards at the ECC Monday thru Friday during the Early Childhood Center's arrival and dismissal times. A portion of the shift will be outdoors, so appropriately dressing for the weather is a must! Tasks & Responsibilities: Applicants must commit to the full semester Complete the provided training\u00a0 Attend every assigned shift\u00a0 Assist ECC families by ensuring a safe crosswalk during arrival and departure times Communication with the ECC Director and Teachers/Staff Assist with small ECC projects, as time allows Qualifications: Excellent communication skills Time management skills Unwavering commitment to attendance Passion for working with children and fostering a positive environment Federal Work Study Recipient (preferred, not required) Potential Future Career Benefit:\u00a0 The ECC Crossing Guard program provides a fulfilling experience for students interested in any field that requires interacting with the public by enhancing communication and interpersonal skills. This position will allow interactions with the ECC staff, enrolled students and their families. Application Instructions : Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: Kerri Robe Commitment: 1-3 hours per week Term: temporary, part-time position \u00a0(Fall-26 & Spring-27)", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200982674066_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Electrician", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-28\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nOhio Wesleyan University ( www.owu.edu ), a selective, private, undergraduate liberal arts, residential institution founded in 1842 and is located just 20 miles north of Columbus, is seeking dynamic,\u00a0 skilled candidates for the position of Electrician . This is a fulltime, hourly position.\u00a0 \u00a0 RESPONSIBILITIES INCLUDE \u2013 BUT NOT LIMITED TO : \u00a0 This individual reports directly to the Electrical Trades Supervisor and is responsible to install, test, and service the electrical light and power distribution circuits, equipment, appliances, fire alarms systems, and other related electrical services at the University. \u00a0 \u00a0This position will also be responsible for the testing and maintaining of life safety systems including but not limited to fire alarm systems and devices,\u00a0 egress lighting, fire extinguishers, elevator emergency phones and other tasks that are code required. This person will be required to keep accurate records. \u00a0 \u00a0 QUALIFICATIONS /SKILLS: \u00a0 A high school diploma or equivalent is required. \u00a0 Also, required is seven years previous experience with commercial/industrial electric or have completed a four-year apprenticeship. \u00a0 The electrician must also have a valid Ohio Driver\u2019s License.\u00a0 Must be capable of independent judgment and be able to be guided by oral or written instructions to complete the associated tasks/responsibilities. \u00a0 \u00a0 Must be able to work from blueprints or sketches. Must have knowledge of electrical codes and standards written by the National Electrical Code, National Fire Protection Agency (particularly Articles 70 & 72), OSHA requirements,\u00a0 and the\u00a0 safe practices associated with this trade. Must be able to lift and handle weights common to this trade and work at heights up to 35 feet from either a scaffold or a ladder. Be on emergency call-in rotation schedule. \u00a0 FACTORS CONTRIBUTING TO SUCCESS: Thorough knowledge of methods, tools, and practices used in the electrical trade Thorough knowledge of the hazards and safety precautions particular to the trade Good communication skills and ability to work effectively with other people Near visual acuity, skill in interpreting technical literature, blueprints, drawings and manufacturer\u2019s instructions Knowledge of Life Safety systems, fire alarms, emergency backup systems and applicable codes WORKING CONDITIONS:\u00a0 May perform work in all University facilities and is subject to possible exposure to chemicals, gases, electrical shock; may work in confined spaces on ladders. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. \u00a0 What We Offer: \u00a0 Ohio Wesleyan University offers a rewarding place to work! \u00a0 To discover why OWU should be your next work home, visit\u00a0 our website . Learn more about our benefits at\u00a0 Discover our Benefits .", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200978524879_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Director of Student Accounts and Bursar", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-15\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nOhio Wesleyan University is seeking an experienced higher education student accounts leader to serve as its Director of Student Accounts and Bursar . This position offers a unique opportunity to combine student financial services expertise, operational leadership, and student engagement to support student success and the University\u2019s mission. The Director of Student Accounts and Bursar reports to the Controller and leads the University\u2019s student accounts operations, including billing, cashiering, collections, account reconciliation, regulatory compliance, and student financial communications. The position also partners across campus to promote financial literacy, assist students and families in understanding their financial responsibilities, and support institutional retention efforts by helping students overcome financial barriers to enrollment and persistence. What You\u2019ll Do As the University\u2019s Director of Student Accounts and Bursar, you will: \u2022 Lead all aspects of student billing, payment processing, cashiering, collections, account holds, and student account operations. \u2022 Ensure the accurate assessment of tuition, fees, payments, payment plans, and refunds, including Title IV credit balances, and complete timely account reconciliations. \u2022 Develop and deliver financial literacy resources and educational programming that support informed financial decision-making. \u2022 Provide financial counseling and payment guidance to students and families while supporting student retention and persistence initiatives. \u2022 Oversee cashiering operations, collection processes, third-party and sponsor billing, and relationships with external payment and collection vendors. \u2022 Serve as the functional administrator for the University\u2019s student accounts system (Power Campus Student Accounts). \u2022 Develop, implement, and maintain internal controls, policies, and procedures that promote financial accuracy, compliance, and operational efficiency, including payment card (PCI) compliance. \u2022 Partner with Financial Aid, Enrollment Management, Student Success, Residential Life, the Registrar, Information Services, and other campus departments to provide exceptional service to students and families. \u2022 Administer IRS Form 1098-T reporting and ensure compliance with applicable federal, state, and institutional regulations, including FERPA. \u2022 Partner with the Controller on month-end reconciliations, year-end close activities, and annual audit preparation. \u2022 Supervise and develop Student Accounts staff fostering accountability, continuous improvement, and outstanding customer service. What We\u2019re Looking For We\u2019re seeking an experienced higher education accounting professional who enjoys solving complex financial challenges while building strong relationships with students, families, and campus partners. Required Qualifications \u2022 Minimum of five years of progressively responsible experience in student accounts, bursar operations, or student financial services within higher education. \u2022 Strong customer service, communication, and interpersonal skills. \u2022 Bachelor\u2019s degree. \u2022 Proficiency with Microsoft Excel and Microsoft Word. \u2022 Ability to prioritize multiple responsibilities while maintaining accuracy and meeting deadlines. Preferred Qualifications Experience in one or more of the following is strongly preferred. We will support the right candidate in learning OWU-specific systems and procedures. \u2022 IRS Form 1098-T reporting and FERPA compliance. \u2022 Power Campus (Ellucian), Microsoft Dynamics GP, Flywire, Nelnet ePayment, or similar higher education enterprise systems. \u2022 Title IV credit balance and refund processing, and coordination with Financial Aid. \u2022 Cashiering, accounts receivable, and collections experience in a higher education setting. \u2022 Financial counseling or financial literacy programming. \u2022 Student retention or student success initiatives. \u2022 Advanced Microsoft Excel skills, including Pivot Tables, XLOOKUP/VLOOKUP, INDEX/MATCH, and data analysis. \u2022 Accounting process improvement, workflow automation, and operational efficiency initiatives and reporting. \u2022 Supervisory experience and staff development. Successful candidates will also demonstrate strong analytical and problem-solving abilities, sound judgment, exceptional organizational skills, and the ability to communicate financial information effectively to students, families, and colleagues from diverse backgrounds. NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Why Ohio Wesleyan? Ohio Wesleyan University is a private liberal arts university in Delaware, Ohio, committed to providing a welcoming, inclusive, and student-centered environment where employees make a meaningful impact every day. As Director of Student Accounts and Bursar, you\u2019ll play an important role in helping students successfully navigate the financial aspects of their education while ensuring the integrity and effectiveness of the University\u2019s student financial operations. If you\u2019re a higher education student financial services professional who works collaboratively, pursues continuous improvement, delivers exceptional customer service, and supports student success, we encourage you to apply and become part of the Ohio Wesleyan community.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200976050179_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Student Worker - Biological Sciences Assistant", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-08\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nStudent Worker \u2013\u00a0 Biological Sciences Assistant \u00a0 Number of Openings: 8 \u00a0 Purpose/Objective of the Role: You will be assisting the Biology Laboratory Coordinators and/or Greenhouse Manager Tasks & Responsibilities:\u00a0 Duties of the Biological Sciences Assistant can include:\u00a0 Helping to set up and break down Biology labs, washing labware, measuring liquid and dry media, restocking lab supplies, animal care, watering plants, testing eye wash stations, repairing equipment, cleaning field lab equipment, assisting StAP and/or Museum Interns with special projects, public science outreach programs, assisting faculty members during Biol 122 laboratory sections (if qualified), following health and safety guidelines.\u00a0 Animal care duties include: providing day to day support for the feeding and housing of departmental invertebrates and fish, checking/recording room temperature and humidity, cleaning fish tanks, making sure that filters, freezers, and refrigerators are operating correctly. Qualifications/Skills: Successful completion of the following courses (may be currently enrolled this semester):\u00a0 Biol 120 (Introduction to Cell Biology)\u00a0 Biol 122 (Organisms & Their Environment) Attention to detail Ability to work well independently and as part of a team Potential Future Career Benefit: Any field in the biological sciences \u00a0 NOTE:\u00a0 Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Application Instructions: \u00a0 Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor:\u00a0 Lisa Tabak Commitment: 3-6 hours per week Term: Full Academic Year (Fall 2026 & Spring 2027), temporary, part-time position", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200976115986_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Student Worker - SIO Desk Assistant", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-08\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nStudent Worker \u2013\u00a0 SIO Desk Assistant\u00a0 Number of Openings: 8 Purpose/Objective of the Role: The OWU Student Involvement Office (SIO) is seeking an enthusiastic, customer service-oriented Desk Assistants to support the daily operations of the SIO Information Desk. This role serves as the first point of contact for students, staff, and visitors. This role provides excellent customer service by assisting with campus inquiries, directing student organizations to appropriate resources, and supporting SIO programs and services. Successful candidates should demonstrate professionalism, strong communication skills, reliability, and a willingness to learn new skills, technology, and campus resources. Tasks & Responsibilities:\u00a0 Attend training sessions and demonstrate proficiency in understanding of the Student Involvement Office\u2019s services, resources, and procedures\u00a0 Support and execute event management details for office events and programs\u00a0 Answer phone calls, direct calls to the correct office/department, and take detailed phone messages\u00a0 Manage online resources including the Student Involvement Office website, email, Engage, and HWCC digital signage\u00a0 Manage and update the SIO social media accounts with information about upcoming training, events, and opportunities to get involved\u00a0 Create and distribute SIO marketing to effectively promote campus events\u00a0 Manage office supplies and spaces to ensure it is kept organized and tidy Qualifications/Skills: An SIO Desk Assistant should have good communication skills, must be dependable and willing to learn, and willing to provide excellent customer service.\u00a0 Must be a current full-time OWU enrolled student and have federal work study. Potential Future Career Benefit: SIO Desk Assistants will gain a variety of transferable skills which include but is not limited to:\u00a0 Communication skills\u00a0 Customer service experience\u00a0 Organizational skills\u00a0 Professionalism\u00a0 Experience learning new technology and office skills NOTE:\u00a0 Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Application Instructions:\u00a0 Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor:\u00a0 Dina Daltorio Commitment: 5 hours/week and additional hours for SIO programming support\u00a0 Term: Full Academic Year (Fall 2026 & Spring 2027), temporary, part-time position", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200966178277_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "GMT - HVAC Technician", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-16\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nAbout the candidate:\u00a0 You are an HVAC tech with license to handle refrigerant who has a passion for building relationships and helping people. You might already have specific experience working in construction or have served in roles in the building trades. You are looking forward to working in a friendly and fast paced role on a college campus, comfortable applying your learned knowledge and skill servicing both residential and commercial facilities.\u00a0 About us:\u00a0 OWU Facilities Services is a dedicated group of trades and general maintenance technicians, dedicated to Ohio Wesleyan University students and the campus we collectively serve. This position has a unique opportunity to work collaboratively with many groups on campus and to be a part of a team that focuses on growing skills and developing employees.\u00a0 Job Summary:\u00a0 Working under general supervision, the incumbent will apply knowledge and skill to repair, install, maintain and troubleshoot heating, ventilation, air conditioning and refrigeration equipment including associated and connected equipment. Complete routine and emergency work orders. Performs preventive maintenance, as assigned. Responsibilities and duties :\u00a0 Supports the efficient operation, maintenance, and testing of the University heating plant, as well as the following systems: steam distribution, pneumatic, hydronic, HVAC, refrigeration, plumbing, and energy management.\u00a0 Aid in the implementation of the preventative/corrective maintenance program.\u00a0 Assist in maintaining supply/inventory levels of shop requirements. Contributes to other trades and area within facilities as needed and directed by supervisor or other leadership within OWU. Helps to coordinate and supervise outside contractors/vendors who provide contractual support for the mechanical trades department functions, such as:\u00a0 Chiller maintenance Boiler maintenance and inspection A/C maintenance Building sprinkler inspections Boiler water treatment PM programs Energy management Reports work rules and safety violations to the supervisor. Performs other duties as assigned. Factors contributing success:\u00a0 High school diploma or GED \u00a0 Vocational or technical training or degree. Universal Refrigerant License/Certification. Strong Commitment to Customer Service and a willingness to contribute across campus to support students, faculty, staff and visitors. Five (5) year\u2019s experience in a related field such as stationary engineer, HVAC, plumbing, or refrigeration. Broad-based background and knowledge of all mechanical trades with an emphasis on HVACR and building automation systems. EPA refrigeration certification. Skill in record keeping. Knowledge and experience of: electrical control systems, motors and motor control, basic wiring methods, soldering/brazing techniques, and commercial kitchen appliances. Knowledge of National, State, and Local mechanical installation, operation, and safety codes. Skill in using MS \u201cWord\u201d and \u201cExcel\u201d software. Prior BAS experience with Delta, Ecostructure, and or Tridium is desired. The individual must also: Possess a valid Ohio driver\u2019s license and ability to pass OWU background check. Posses a Universal license for refrigerant. Be able to lift weights common to trade. Be able to work at heights common to trade. Be on an emergency call-in rotation schedule. Must be able to be contacted 24/7 during assigned on call schedule. NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. \u00a0 What We Offer: Ohio Wesleyan University offers a rewarding place to work! To discover why OWU should be your next work home, visit\u00a0 our website . Learn more about our benefits at\u00a0 Discover our Benefits .", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200947521006_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Student Worker - Bishop Scholars Tutor", "description": "Posted: 2026-04-28\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nPurpose/Objective of the Role:\u00a0 The Bishop Scholars Program seeks energized and committed students to tutor elementary youth in Delaware City Schools, Columbus City Schools, and Columbus Bilingual Academy North for the fall, 2026 and spring, 2027 semesters. Tutoring days include Monday,Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday with various tutoring times from approximately 8:15 a.m.\u2013 4:00 p.m. This is a PAID position and all potential tutors must complete an in-person interview, criminal background check, and mandatory training prior to being accepted into the program. Transportation to and from our partnering schools will be provided. Tasks & Responsibilities:\u00a0 Must commit to the full semester! Attend assigned day(s) of tutoring. Be on time! University transportation will leave at designated time. We will not wait for you. Wear appropriate dress attire, as outlined by OWU and our partner school guidelines. Must wear a Bishop Scholars or OWU branded shirt. Meet with assigned elementary students each scheduled day and actively interact & tutor in core competencies outlined by the partner school (Math and Reading, primarily). Complete student tutor logs each assigned day of tutoring.\u00a0 Communicate attendance or program concerns to the Bishop Scholars Director at least two (2) hours prior to campus departure . Actively participate in on-campus training(s) and Lunch-and-Learns. Share the mission and work of the Bishop Scholars Program with peers in the campus community. Represent the Bishop Scholars Program on campus at Connection Conferences, symposiums, and recruitment events. Participate in and complete program surveys and reflections. Work hours must be entered into ADP on your assigned tutoring day. Qualifications: Excellent Communication Skills Time Management Skills Effective Written skills Unwavering Commitment to Attendance Strong team player with the ability to adapt to diverse team/school participants Passion for working with children and fostering a positive learning environment Spanish Speaking (preferred for one partner school, but not required) Federal Work Study Recipient (preferred, not required) \u00a0 Potential Future Career Benefit: The Bishop Scholars Program provides excellent experience for students interested in the Education, Medical, or any field that requires working with the public by enhancing communication, written and interpersonal skills. Experience will include working with both children and professional staff. NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Application Instructions : Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: Kerri Robe Commitment: 3-8 hours per week Term: temporary, part-time position \u00a0( Fall 2026 & Spring 2027 )", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200945540777_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Student Worker - Teachers Aide", "description": "Posted: 2026-04-22\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nStudent Worker \u2013\u00a0Teacher\u2019s Aide (Fall 26 & Spring 27) \u00a0 Purpose/Objective of the Role:\u00a0 \u00a0 The Early Childhood Center is a community preschool and university lab school enrolling children between the ages of three and five years of age. \u00a0 Student staff serve as teacher\u2019s aides and gain valuable experiences working directly with young children and their families. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Tasks & Responsibilities:\u00a0 \u00a0 Assisting the head classroom teacher with the following activities:\u00a0 Outdoor play Snack time Daily instructional activities Work as a team with other student staff and head classroom teachers . \u00a0 Qualifications:\u00a0 \u00a0 Experience working with young children Completion of successful FBI and BCI background check\u00a0 Completion of ODJFS medical exam\u00a0 Certification in Infant/child CPR and First Aid \u00a0 \u00a0 Potential Future Career Benefit:\u00a0 \u00a0 Classroom teaching experience (education)\u00a0 Interacting with children and families (psychology)\u00a0 Assisting/participating in large motor classroom activities (HHK) \u00a0 Note: \u00a0Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Application Instructions : Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: Kellie Hall Commitment: Varies Term: Full Academic Year (Fall 26 & Spring 27) temporary, part-time position", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200751841909_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Assistant Wrestling Coach", "description": "Posted: 2024-11-19\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nOhio Wesleyan University invites applications for the position of Assistant Coach -\u00a0 Wrestling . The assistant coach is responsible for supporting the Head Coach in all phases of the wrestling program. \u00a0 The assistant coach will provide support to the head coach focused primarily on recruiting and will have event coaching responsibilities. \u00a0The assistant coach will be responsible for involvement in current and future leadership of the program administrative assistance and coaching. \u00a0 \u00a0Additional duties will include but not limited to skill development, academic advising, mentoring, one on one and group instruction, summer camps/clinics, and daily operations of the program. \u00a0 \u00a0It is also expected that the Wrestling Assistant Coach will embrace the department mission of supporting the academic mission of the university, developing student-athletes as contributors to the greater community, creating opportunities for competitive success, leading student-athletes to understand what it is like to be part of something greater than oneself. \u00a0 \u00a0 Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s Degree\u00a0 Previous successful coaching experience\u00a0 Familiarity in recruiting collegiate student-athletes Articulated commitment to the highest standards of professional and ethical behavior and to adhering to all rules and regulations of Ohio Wesleyan University, the North Coast Athletic Conference, and the NCAA. \u00a0 Effective written communication skills Student-centered focus\u00a0 CPR, First Aid and AED Certification is required (and can be completed after hire) \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree\u00a0 Ability to articulate the role that athletics plays in a rigorous academic collegiate setting and the importance of academic endeavors of student athletes Successful recruiting experience at the college or university level, with ability to identify and attract outstanding\u00a0students and players Experience exhibiting the highest standards of professional and ethical behavior and adhering to all rules and regulations of Ohio Wesleyan University, the North Coast Athletic Conference, and the NCAA. \u00a0 \u00a0 Experience advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion, and supporting students from diverse backgrounds. Ability to actively foster a respectful, positive environment that welcomes all persons. An appreciation for and willingness to engage with the mission and aims of OWU. \u00a0 Completed application packets will include: 1) \u00a0 Cover Letter\u00a0 2) \u00a0 Resume or Curriculum Vitae\u00a0 3) \u00a0 The names, titles, and contact information for three professional references \u00a0Application review will begin immediately and will continue until position is filled. \u00a0 \u00a0 WHAT WE OFFER: Ohio Wesleyan University offers a rewarding place to work! To discover why this should be your next work home, visit our website . Learn more about our benefits at Discover our Benefits . As an equal opportunity institution, OWU has a commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and anti-racism. We do not discriminate on any basis including: race, religion, color, culture, national origin, sex and/or sexual orientation, gender, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status, economic barriers, or any other legally protected factor. NOTE: \u00a0Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200667532299_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Background Screening", "description": "Posted: 2024-05-10\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nBackground Screening APP/Consent for OWU Camps & Events", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200655037867_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "General Maintenance Technician", "description": "Posted: 2024-04-10\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nOhio Wesleyan University is a selective, private, undergraduate liberal art, residential institution founded in 1842 and located just 20 miles north of Columbus OH, is seeking candidates for two positions: \u00a0A licensed Plumber and a General Maintenance Technician with a plumbing focus. \u00a0We welcome positive, friendly and self-motivated candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our campus community. \u00a0 About you:\u00a0 You are a licensed plumber or a seasoned maintenance technician who has a passion for building relationships and helping people. You might already have specific experience working in construction or have served in roles in the building trades. \u00a0You are looking forward to working in a friendly and fast paced role on a college campus, comfortable applying your earned knowledge and skill servicing both residential and commercial facilities.\u00a0 About us: \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Campus Buildings and Grounds are a dedicated group of trades and general maintenance technicians, dedicated to Ohio Wesleyan University students and the campus we collectively serve. \u00a0This position has a unique opportunity to work collaboratively with many groups on campus and to be a part of a team that focuses on growing skills and developing employees. \u00a0 \u00a0 Job Summary:\u00a0 Working under general supervision, the incumbent will apply knowledge and skill at the journey level to install and repair piping, fixtures, appliances, laboratory equipment, and apparatus related to gas, air, steam, water, drainage systems, and heating and cooling systems. Complete routine and emergency work orders. Performs preventive maintenance, as assigned. \u00a0 Factors contributing success:\u00a0 \u00a0 At least five years plumbing experience in both commercial and residential construction, as well as a Plumbing Commercial Contractor\u2019s license granted by the State of Ohio Valid driver's license and ability to meet OWU Driving Policy. a backflow tester license granted by the State of Ohio.Experience performing preventative and predictive maintenance of building systems equipment Ability to use equipment and tools effectively to perform essential job functions, demonstrate basic computer skills in order to communicate in writing as well as procure parts and interact with the computerized maintenance management system. Ability to work with and around a diverse culture \u00a0Completed application packets will include: 1) \u00a0 Cover Letter with salary requirements 2) \u00a0 Resume or Curriculum Vitae \u00a0WHAT WE OFFER: \u00a0Ohio Wesleyan University offers a rewarding place to work! To discover why this should be your next work home, visit our website . Learn more about our benefits at Discover our Benefits .", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200383744301_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "PT Faculty", "description": "Posted: 2022-04-27\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nTo move forward in the OWU new hire process, you will need to complete this system setup within ADP. This system also serves as our applicant tracking system. However, you are not considered a new applicant. Please do not be concerned by the use of the word applicant. Ultimately, the information you enter is needed to run a pre-employment background check. Once your background check is successfully completed, your new employee payroll record will also be established within this system. For any questions about this system or the OWU new hire process, please contact Human Resources at hr@owu.edu or 740/368-3388.\u00a0 WHAT WE OFFER: Ohio Wesleyan University offers a rewarding place to work! To discover why this should be your next work home, visit\u00a0 our website . Learn more about our benefits at\u00a0 Discover our Benefits . As an equal opportunity institution, OWU has a commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and anti-racism. We do not discriminate on any basis including: race, religion, color, culture, national origin, sex and/or sexual orientation, gender, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status, economic barriers, or any other legally protected factor. NOTE: \u00a0Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Candidates who accept offers of employment must be able to provide proof of their vaccination status before their employment can be process.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201869022987_2&lang=en_US": {"title": "Research Fellow-SW", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nStudent Worker \u2013\u00a0 Research Fellow \u00a0 Number of Openings: 1 \u00a0 Purpose/Objective of the Role:\u00a0 A local nonprofit is rebranding and is interested in determining how effective this effort is. To gauge whether awareness of the nonprofit\u2019s services have increased, they need a baseline measure of awareness. Working with the Community Research Fellows program at OWU, the selected students will design and conduct a market research survey of Delaware residents to glean this information from the community. \u00a0 Tasks & Responsibilities: The Fellow would travel within Delaware County to conduct the survey, analyze the responses, and summarize the results for the client in a remote meeting. Qualifications/Skills:\u00a0 \u00a0 The Fellow must be skilled in interpersonal communication and be able to convince a sufficient number of respondents to complete a brief, in-person survey. The Fellow must be an effective writer and also be able to integrate graphs, figures, and images into a report for the client. The Fellow needs to have their own vehicle and driver\u2019s license in order to travel to multiple locations within Delaware County in order to conduct the survey.\u00a0 All students with familiarity with surveys are invited to apply. Applicants are asked to send a copy of your transcript, your resume, a cover letter explaining detailing your interest, and a writing to sample to Prof. Georgic at wcgeorgic@owu.edu . Applicants are urged to apply quickly so interviews and work can begin soon. Potential Future Career Benefit:\u00a0 \u00a0 The fellow will gain market research experience under the guidance of Prof. Georgic and the Community Research Fellows Program. NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. \u00a0 Application Instructions:\u00a0 \u00a0 Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor:\u00a0 Will Georgic Commitment: 5 - hours per week Term: Fall 2026 and Spring 2027 , part-time position", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201849320162_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Videographer Intern-SW", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-25\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nStudent Worker - Videographer Intern (Marketing and Communications)\u00a0 Number of Openings: 1 \u00a0 Purpose/Objective of the Role: This student will support Ohio Wesleyan University\u2019s Marketing & Communications team by developing and producing video content that tells the OWU story. The intern will capture and edit videos for use in social media, and admission marketing, helping prospective students, alumni, and the wider community connect with the university. \u00a0 Tasks & Responsibilities: Film high-quality, compelling video stories featuring OWU students, faculty, staff, and alumni. Edit short-form and long-form video content for social media, web, and promotional use. Help manage OWU\u2019s YouTube content. Brainstorm creative content ideas in collaboration with the Marketing & Communications team. Stay attuned to video and social media trends to suggest fresh approaches. Assist with video needs at special events\u00a0 \u00a0 Qualifications/Skills: Interest in video production, digital media, or storytelling. Experience with video editing software (Adobe Premiere Pro, Final Cut Pro, CapCut, or similar). Understanding of camera operation, lighting, and audio (training provided if needed). Strong organizational skills and ability to balance multiple projects. Creativity, curiosity, and an eye for capturing authentic, engaging moments. Good communication skills and willingness to work collaboratively. Proven ability to manage multiple short-term and long-term projects, prioritize. Turn around video projects quickly\u00a0 o meet deadlines, while producing high-quality, compelling videos. Proven ability, and perform well on deadline as well as on long-term projects. \u00a0 Potential Future Career Benefit: This internship is ideal for any student interested in video production, filmmaking, multimedia storytelling, social media, and/or marketing. NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States \u00a0 Application Instructions : Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: Kiona Dyches Commitment: 6 hours per week Term: Full Academic Year ( Fall & Spring ), temporary, part-time position", "department": ""}}, "rows": {"https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201864354637_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 1047, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201864354637_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Part Time Spanish Instructor", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "Department of World Languages and Cultures", "area_key_words": "Spanish", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-10-09", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201858549405_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 1047, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201858549405_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Public Safety Officer Part Time", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-09-22", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201856646448_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 1047, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201856646448_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Data Science Research Assistant-SW", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-09-16", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201853792179_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 1047, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201853792179_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Accounting Operation